    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Symbotic Inc. is a public company headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts, traded under the ticker SYM. On its own site, the company describes itself as a provider of end-to-end warehouse automation for retailers and distributors, and as the software and key robotic innovator behind each of its systems. It says its systems combine dense storage, streamlined operations, and AI-enhanced software, and that its solutions can handle goods ranging from 1 lb (0.5 kg) and 2 x 6.4 x 5 in (5.1 x 16.3 x 12.7 cm) up to 60 lb (27.2 kg) and 36 x 24 x 16.2 in (91.4 x 61 x 41.2 cm), including loose items and cold chain requirements. The company also describes itself as a leader in industrial automation and in technology at large.\n\nThe site presents the company's AI position as software that expands operational possibilities and, in its words, sees beyond the warehouse walls. It frames its offering against typical integrators, which it says are limited by their portfolio of technology partnerships and cannot resolve problems when those technologies misalign, while Symbotic provides complete, turnkey-ready automation.\n\nThe record shows no lawsuits and no MCP servers associated with the company. Its law exposure is recorded in Massachusetts, with a count of 191.",
